📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates the design and implementation of a small-scale cybersecurity homelab using virtualization technology.

The lab consists of two virtual machines:

Attacker Machine: A Linux-based system used to perform authorized security assessments, network reconnaissance, and penetration-testing exercises.
Target Machine: A Windows-based system used to study system security, network exposure, vulnerabilities, and defensive mechanisms.

Both machines are deployed in Oracle VM VirtualBox and connected through an Internal Network to establish an isolated communication environment.

The primary objective is to understand how security assessments are conducted in practice, how systems communicate over networks, and how defensive controls can be evaluated in a controlled environment.
